  "reasoning": "The claim was submitted 25 days ago and is currently pending adjudication with no payer response on the table. Since the primary payer has not yet issued a determination (neither a payment nor a denial), it is premature to bill the patient or the secondary payer, as the contractual patient share and secondary responsibility cannot be calculated until the primary adjudication is complete. Actions like appealing or requesting peer-to-peer are invalid without a denial, and resubmitting would risk a duplicate claim denial. Therefore, the only appropriate action to progress the claim without violating payer rules is to escalate to a human specialist to monitor the pending status or determine if a status check is needed, as no other available action can properly advance a pending claim.",
